hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20319","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that a man fell upon the slave girl of his wife, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: If she obeyed him, she belongs to him and upon him is the like of her for her, and if he forced her, she is free and upon him is the like of her for her."
"20320","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Jawn ibn Qatadah from Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a house in front of which was a hanging waterskin, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for drink. They said: It is carrion. He said: Its tanning is its slaughter."
"20321","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from a man he named from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon the people of a house and asked for water, and there was a waterskin with water in it. They said: It is carrion, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The hide, its purification is its tanning."
"20322","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Said meaning Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that a man covered the slave girl of his wife while he was on campaign, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: If he forced her, she is free from his wealth and upon him is buying her for her mistress, and if she obeyed him, then the like of her from his wealth for her mistress."
"20323","Ismail narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that a man went out on campaign with a slave girl of his wife with him, and he fell upon her, and it was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: If he forced her, she is freed and for her is upon him the like of her, and if she obeyed him, she is his maid and for her is upon him the like of her. And Ismail once said: A man was on campaign."
"20324","Hushaym narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning."
"20325","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20326","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Jawn ibn Qatadah from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a waterskin on the day of Hunayn and called for water from it, and with it was a woman. She said: It is carrion. He said: Ask her, has it not been tanned? She said: Yes. Then he took from it for his need and said: The slaughter of the hide is its tanning."
"20327","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Jawn ibn Qatadah from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Tabuk, and he came upon a house in front of which was a hanging waterskin, and he asked for drink. It was said: It is carrion. He said: Its slaughter is its tanning."
"20328","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Qabisah ibn Hurayth from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning a man who had intercourse with the slave girl of his wife: If he forced her, she is free and upon him for her mistress is the like of her."
"20329","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq informed me from Muadh ibn Sawah al-Rasibi from Sinan ibn Salamah al-Hudhali from his father Salamah, and he had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sent two sacrificial camels with a man and said: If anything happens to them, slaughter them and dip the sandal in their blood, then strike with it their sides so it may be known that they are sacrificial camels, he said: The side of each one. He said: And do not eat from them, you nor anyone of your company, and leave them for those after you."
"20330","Amr ibn al-Haytham and Abu Dawud and Abd al-Samad with the meaning narrated to us, they said: Hisham informed us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Jawn ibn Qatadah from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water from a waterskin with a woman. She said: It is carrion. He said: Have you not tanned it? She said: Yes. He said: Its tanning is its slaughter."
"20331","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Habib al-Awdhi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: We campaigned with Sinan ibn Salamah in Mukran, and Sinan ibn Salamah said: My father Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is overtaken by Ramadan having a mount carrying him to satiety, let him fast Ramadan wherever it overtakes him."
"20332","And Sinan said: I was born on the day of Hunayn, and my father was given glad tidings of me, and they said to him: A boy has been born to you. He said: An arrow with which I shoot on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is dearer to me than what you have given me glad tidings of. And he named me Sinan."
